  "tagline": "Kubernetes-native distributed vector search engine built on Yahoo Japan's NGT.",
  "description": "Vald is a distributed approximate nearest neighbour search engine created at Yahoo Japan (now LY Corporation) and designed to run only on Kubernetes. It uses the NGT graph index, shards vectors across agent pods, rebuilds indexes asynchronously without blocking queries and backs index state up to persistent volumes or object storage. Filtering and pre/post-processing are handled by pluggable gRPC 'filter' components. It is solid infrastructure for teams already deep in Kubernetes, but it has a much smaller community than Milvus or Qdrant and no metadata-rich query layer.",
